The [light-theme raw interaction video](https://media.aylith.com/proomptal/media/i17-source-library-2026-09-25-7e394b5/raw-light.webm) and [dark-theme raw interaction video](https://media.aylith.com/proomptal/media/i17-source-library-2026-09-25-7e394b5/raw-dark.webm) are short **silent actual browser recordings** of entry → search → detail → copy. They begin on the first-view hero, not the populated cards; the dark raw clip includes a brief real loading frame and compression. The paired Library stills separately prove the saved-card state. These raw videos are diagnostic footage, not polished, narrated or captioned release films.

The same fictional SQLite fixture was listed, searched and shown by the Bun CLI; its exact text output, browser/API receipts and all media hashes are preserved with the media source. No packaged AI-tool installation, prompt revision history, semantic search, cross-device sync or hosted account is demonstrated. Cartesia narration, Remotion light/dark final films, timed captions and a final approved cover remain open.
